                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coup d'état; an illegal effort to forcibly overthrow the current government."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8728bf47-d05c-47f3-950b-f6b565de8ef2",
                                                "sense_id": "e9558cac-ef0d-397f-9ca6-3dadb12083fa",
                                                "text": "Afterward, the ringleaders of the failed putsch were publicly executed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec8a8069-3d7a-4e5f-8ba6-1ec90814acd7",
                                                "sense_id": "e9558cac-ef0d-397f-9ca6-3dadb12083fa",
                                                "text": "2010, Thompson, M. 2010. Modernisation theory’s last redoubt: democratisation in east and south east Asia. In Yin-wah Chu and Siu-lun Wong (ed), 'East Asia's new democracies: deepening, reversal, non-liberal alternatives'. London, Routledge.p98.\n\"They have broken the democratic rules of the game by supporting popular mobilisation that has resulted in what can be dubbed a \"people power putsch\".\""
                                            }
